WEBVTT

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:28.150
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:28.150
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:28.150
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:53.730 --> 00:02:02.150
The Retriever
Chapter IV

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:08.310
Having taken a alternate route based on data provided by the Imperial Military Liaison Officer at Phezzan...

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:13.550
...Reinhard succeeded in
evading the Alliance blockade...

00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:15.650
...and was closing in
on Iserlohn Corridor.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:19.610
But trouble is waiting for
us from this point on.

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:21.600
Regardless of which course we take...

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:25.210
...it's evident that we'll eventually
have to head to Iserlohn Corridor...

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:29.550
...so the enemy will most certainly 
blockade our entry into the Corridor.

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:33.250
Since we can't use a feint operation similar to the one we used when we made our entry...

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:36.990
...we must believe that it will be
extremely difficult to break through{the blockade}.

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:42.160
Moreover, there is the issue of supplies.

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:47.870
Since we've veered far away from our initial course, both fuel and supplies are running low.

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:53.700
As is, we may make it inside the Corridor, but if we can't get resupplied there...

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:57.450
...we could end up being cut off in the middle of enemy territory.

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:02.470
What do you think, Captain ?

00:03:02.470 --> 00:03:07.550
The orders we had included
the capture of Count Helksheimer...

00:03:07.550 --> 00:03:10.520
...and retrieval of the military
secret he was smuggling.

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:18.350
We could not secure the person of the Count, but his death has been confirmed.

00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:22.550
The only task left is bringing back the directional Seffle Particle generator.

00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:28.500
So I plan to make a deal with the Count's orphaned daughter, Lady Margareta.

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:33.400
We'll release her and the ship...

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:35.700
...and in exchange, we'll have 
her give us the access code.

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:38.750
Then we'll transfer the
equipment to this ship.

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:39.910
Please wait.

00:03:39.910 --> 00:03:41.230
We have orders...

00:03:41.230 --> 00:03:42.910
And we're not violating them{by this action}.

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:53.110
It may feel a bit like sophistry,
but I think you're right.

00:03:53.110 --> 00:03:54.450
Upon doing that...

00:03:54.450 --> 00:04:00.350
...you plan to use the directional control 
program to penetrate the blockade, correct ?

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:07.900
Then why don't we make that proposal and just get the access code out of her first ?

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:11.500
After that, we can do whatever we need to do with her.

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:13.790
That would be dishonorable.

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:17.260
Um, no, I don't mean we'll deceive her.

00:04:17.260 --> 00:04:22.680
I just don't know if it's a good idea
to let a ten year old girl defect alone.

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:24.150
We should take her
back to the homeland...

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:27.730
...leave her to her relatives, 
or find an appropriate guardian...

00:04:28.190 --> 00:04:30.720
LTJG Kircheis, explain it to him.

00:04:32.110 --> 00:04:38.900
Kircheis explained that a Court conflict
appeared to be hidden behind this defection.

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:45.050
That because of it, her life could be in danger if she were taken back to the homeland.

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:49.700
For that reason, she might not have anyone
who would be willing to become her guardian.

00:04:50.650 --> 00:04:54.450
And the information that
caused this series of events...

00:04:54.450 --> 00:04:58.250
...appears to be hidden inside
the protected program.

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:06.800
Lt. Commander, you knew
about this, didn't you ?

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:08.450
"This" ?

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:09.960
What do you mean ?

00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:11.030
Don't feign ignorance.

00:05:11.030 --> 00:05:13.110
You were not just an inspector.

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:17.250
You had secret orders to retrieve or destroy the information...

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:22.240
...without our knowledge when
we recovered the equipment.

00:05:22.930 --> 00:05:25.980
I'm insulted at such an insinuation, I...

00:05:25.980 --> 00:05:28.550
You weren't informed of its contents.

00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:31.150
You were forbidden
to view the contents.

00:05:31.150 --> 00:05:32.390
Isn't that true ?

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:38.110
You were merely trying
to obey your orders.

00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:43.650
You weren't siding with schemers who would target and murder a young girl, and the like.

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:46.310
You'd feel grieved to be
misunderstood that way, wouldn't you ?

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:49.110
All right.

00:05:49.110 --> 00:05:53.870
In any case, with this proposal, we'll have Lady Margareta tell us the access code.

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:57.080
We'll decide what to do after we
view the contents of the information.

00:05:57.820 --> 00:05:59.240
That should suit you, 
Lt. Commander, correct ?

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:01.660
As you wish...

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:09.480
I understand.

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:11.400
I'll trust you all.

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:15.900
Especially you, Siegfried.

00:06:17.150 --> 00:06:18.020
I'm honored.

00:06:23.450 --> 00:06:24.390
This is it.

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:40.000
Kircheis, you aren't going to
say you want to protect that girl...

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:43.190
...and defect with her
to the Alliance, are you ?

00:06:43.190 --> 00:06:44.140
Lord Reinhard.

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:01.060
We did it.

00:07:04.850 --> 00:07:05.690
This must be it.

00:07:06.620 --> 00:07:07.630
Shall we open it ?

00:07:07.630 --> 00:07:08.210
Yes.

00:07:11.870 --> 00:07:12.920
This is...?

00:07:15.210 --> 00:07:18.550
A surprising fact was
hidden inside the file.

00:07:18.550 --> 00:07:22.550
Count Helksheimer, under
orders from Marquis Littenheim...

00:07:22.550 --> 00:07:26.200
...was searching for vulnerabilities of his political enemy, Prince Braunschweig{of Littenheim}.

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:30.150
He discovered that Prince
Braunschweig's daughter, Elizabeth...

00:07:30.150 --> 00:07:33.450
...had the characteristics
of a genetic disease.

00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:35.450
When he happily reported
that to Marquis Littenheim...

00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:39.550
...Helksheimer did not
 realize the hidden danger.

00:07:39.550 --> 00:07:42.350
That is, since their
mothers are sisters...

00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:46.650
...those characteristics were also passed on to Marquis Littenheim's daughter, Sabine.

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:49.850
As decreed by Rudolph, the first
Kaiser of the Galactic Empire...

00:07:49.850 --> 00:07:53.400
...if this was disclosed, under the
elimination of inferior genetics law...

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:58.500
...neither Sabine nor Elizabeth would
be able to take the throne as Kaiserin.

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:03.690
Moreover, it also meant the downfall of Marquis Littenheim himself.

00:08:03.690 --> 00:08:10.360
Marquis Littenheim attempted to poison the Helksheimer family to protect the secret.

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:15.140
Captain, I'd like permission to leave the ship.

00:08:17.350 --> 00:08:19.750
What are you saying, so suddenly ?

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:23.450
I have been wearied 
by this present mission.

00:08:23.450 --> 00:08:25.400
I will leave military service, too.

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:29.350
I will become the guardian of 
Lady Margareta and defect with her.

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:34.610
Hey, do you realize 
what you're saying ?

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:36.450
To leave military service...

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:40.200
...you couldn't object if you were executed on the charge of desertion under enemy fire.

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:42.190
Hold on a moment, No. 1.

00:08:42.190 --> 00:08:43.450
But...

00:08:43.450 --> 00:08:46.340
If you defect, what
happens to your family ?

00:08:46.340 --> 00:08:50.450
I'm the third child of
a Baron, and I'm single.

00:08:50.450 --> 00:08:54.190
I have no lineage to preserve, and I have no encumbrances.

00:08:54.190 --> 00:08:58.290
But in the case of defection, your parents will be held responsible.

00:08:58.290 --> 00:08:59.340
Well...

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:05.520
Then please report to the 
homeland that I died in battle.

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:06.650
Hey !

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:09.390
Are you sure you're fine with that ?

00:09:09.390 --> 00:09:10.190
Yes.

00:09:11.730 --> 00:09:12.650
All right.

00:09:13.090 --> 00:09:14.150
Captain !

00:09:14.150 --> 00:09:15.720
It's okay.

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:19.450
Lady Margareta definitely 
needs a guardian.

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:22.040
If this is what he wants, that's good.

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:25.270
Lt. Commander Bendling
went missing in action.

00:09:25.270 --> 00:09:27.690
That will be the official record.

00:09:27.690 --> 00:09:34.050
This, as well as the contents of the file, will remain strictly confidential.

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:35.510
Understood ?

00:09:35.510 --> 00:09:37.660
If you say so.

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:39.870
Thank you.

00:09:46.040 --> 00:09:52.000
The military brass who gave us these orders -
I wonder how much they knew about this ?

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:53.340
I don't know.

00:09:53.340 --> 00:09:56.160
I don't know where the
orders came from, either.

00:09:56.770 --> 00:10:00.320
What do you plan to do with this information, Captain ?

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:02.400
I don't know that, either.

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:06.780
At least you should pretend that you don't know of any of this.

00:10:06.780 --> 00:10:09.250
Otherwise, your life will be in danger.

00:10:10.240 --> 00:10:14.160
As long as I'm a military officer,
I do not mind danger to my life.

00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:18.910
But in any case, we can't worry about
this till after we reach Iserlohn Corridor.

00:10:18.910 --> 00:10:21.600
Right now, we must penetrate the enemy in front of us.

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:22.940
You're right.

00:10:22.940 --> 00:10:25.000
What's the status on the
transfer of the equipment ?

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:27.460
It should be completed by now.

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:48.230
Fraulein, I can't let you go alone.

00:10:48.230 --> 00:10:50.910
You mean you won't 
allow my defection ?

00:10:50.910 --> 00:10:55.780
No, that's not what I meant, but that
Lt. Commander Bendling will accompany you.

00:10:57.230 --> 00:10:59.250
Oh, so a watchdog ?

00:11:00.350 --> 00:11:05.750
In order for you to live in a foreign country, you'll need someone to take care of you.

00:11:05.750 --> 00:11:08.000
Consider him your guardian.

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:10.290
Is he a retainer, or a servant ?

00:11:10.290 --> 00:11:12.800
I don't mind if you 
think of me that way.

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:18.090
You don't seem as 
considerate as Siegfried.

00:11:18.090 --> 00:11:21.540
Siegfried, I'd rather 
have you come with me.

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:30.570
I would have liked to.

00:11:30.570 --> 00:11:37.440
But regrettably, I have already promised someone that I will follow him forever.

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:38.930
I cannot break that oath.

00:11:40.180 --> 00:11:41.660
Is that someone this Captain ?

00:11:44.590 --> 00:11:45.340
Yes.

00:11:45.930 --> 00:11:48.030
You called yourself
Captain Musel, right ?

00:11:48.030 --> 00:11:52.360
For you, is this Siegfried
your retainer, or a servant ?

00:11:54.840 --> 00:11:57.770
He's a friend, an irreplaceable one.

00:12:07.320 --> 00:12:10.290
Then I'll resign myself.

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:11.560
Bendling ?

00:12:11.560 --> 00:12:12.810
Yes, ma'am.

00:12:12.810 --> 00:12:16.250
I hear that there is no class hierarchy in the foreign country we're heading for.

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:20.900
I want you to be my friend, too -
not a retainer or a servant.

00:12:25.850 --> 00:12:27.500
I will be happy to.

00:12:28.850 --> 00:12:30.000
Then shall we go ?

00:12:33.430 --> 00:12:35.950
Oh, Siegfried, wait a minute.

00:12:46.300 --> 00:12:49.380
You said your birthday
is coming up soon.

00:12:49.380 --> 00:12:50.650
I will give this to you.

00:12:51.380 --> 00:12:52.530
This is...?

00:12:53.010 --> 00:12:56.200
I made it, modeling
it after Siegfried.

00:12:56.970 --> 00:12:58.650
Oh, not you.

00:12:59.570 --> 00:13:01.380
It's this Siegfried.

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:03.550
It didn't have a name, 
so that's the name I gave it.

00:13:05.060 --> 00:13:06.530
I'm honored, Fraulein.

00:13:10.030 --> 00:13:11.700
Then take care.

00:13:12.510 --> 00:13:13.840
You too, Fraulein.

00:13:34.350 --> 00:13:37.450
I wonder if this was
the right thing to do.

00:13:37.450 --> 00:13:38.700
I can't say.

00:13:38.700 --> 00:13:43.010
But Lt. Commander Bendling seems to be a sincere man, more so than we thought.

00:13:43.010 --> 00:13:44.200
Let's count on him.

00:13:44.620 --> 00:13:47.200
If you say so, Kircheis.

00:13:47.200 --> 00:13:49.620
But Lady Margareta - what a girl.

00:13:49.620 --> 00:13:52.850
And she's only ten years old.
I wonder what she'll grow up to be like.

00:13:52.850 --> 00:13:56.230
In the Alliance, women
fight on the front lines, too.

00:13:56.230 --> 00:14:00.250
Ten years from now, we might see her on the battlefield.

00:14:00.250 --> 00:14:01.890
That will be troublesome.

00:14:01.890 --> 00:14:05.280
Before that happens, let's bring the universe under my rule.

00:14:08.330 --> 00:14:09.960
Ten years...

00:14:25.830 --> 00:14:27.620
The enemy fleet is
deploying in front of us !

00:14:28.420 --> 00:14:30.350
Prepare the directional Seffle Particles.

00:14:31.750 --> 00:14:34.600
The Seffle Particles 
themselves cannot be controlled.

00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:38.550
Nanomachines that attract Seffle
Particles are mixed in and released...

00:14:38.550 --> 00:14:40.180
...and that's what we control remotely.

00:14:41.110 --> 00:14:47.050
But the number of nanomachines
is limited since this is a test unit.

00:14:47.050 --> 00:14:49.530
At best, we can use it only once.

00:14:50.460 --> 00:14:53.250
Moreover, according to
the data we just obtained...

00:14:53.250 --> 00:14:57.480
...the directionality's success
rate is slightly better than 50%.

00:14:57.480 --> 00:14:59.650
It's better than 50-50, correct ?

00:14:59.650 --> 00:15:01.250
Barely.

00:15:01.250 --> 00:15:03.550
Then we'll gamble on it.

00:15:03.550 --> 00:15:05.650
Right now, we have
no other choice.

00:15:08.150 --> 00:15:10.570
7,000 till the enemy blockade line.

00:15:10.570 --> 00:15:12.750
The enemy is advancing toward us.

00:15:12.750 --> 00:15:15.350
Release the directional Seffle Particles.

00:15:16.110 --> 00:15:16.840
Releasing.

00:15:24.650 --> 00:15:27.720
Vector toward x-axis, plus 90.

00:15:32.790 --> 00:15:33.500
No good ?

00:15:37.840 --> 00:15:39.250
Please, go.

00:15:44.360 --> 00:15:45.700
It's a success.

00:15:45.700 --> 00:15:47.020
Good. Just like that.

00:15:58.090 --> 00:16:00.000
Captain, our energy
is decreasing rapidly !

00:16:03.180 --> 00:16:05.260
The Seffle Particle generator !

00:16:05.870 --> 00:16:06.900
Kircheis !

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:09.650
The energy consumption
is greater than anticipated.

00:16:09.650 --> 00:16:12.770
I suspect there's a problem with the power source connections - I'm investigating it.

00:16:14.240 --> 00:16:16.550
We won't make it - we'll reach the limit in five seconds.

00:16:16.550 --> 00:16:18.000
Shut down the system !

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:18.810
Roger !

00:16:27.100 --> 00:16:28.550
Is it enough...?

00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:30.460
It's enough to create a hole.

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:32.700
While advancing at maximum speed, prepare to fire the main cannon.

00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:38.700
How's our energy ?

00:16:39.500 --> 00:16:41.850
If we fire the main cannon once, there won't be any left.

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:43.590
This is our last gamble.

00:16:43.590 --> 00:16:44.760
Main cannon, fire !

00:16:51.250 --> 00:16:51.900
Go !

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:53.250
Maintain course and charge !

00:16:58.320 --> 00:17:00.050
We've penetrated the enemy line !

00:17:01.990 --> 00:17:02.850
Our energy is...

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:07.900
Switch to auxiliary power.

00:17:09.150 --> 00:17:11.980
Now escape into the
Corridor with inertial flight.

00:17:16.270 --> 00:17:17.220
Captain.

00:17:17.220 --> 00:17:18.010
Good job.

00:17:18.010 --> 00:17:19.650
Now help the Chief Missileer.

00:17:19.650 --> 00:17:21.710
We can't use the
main cannon anymore.

00:17:21.710 --> 00:17:24.450
To deal with enemy pursuers, we'll have to use the mines.

00:17:25.910 --> 00:17:28.090
The explosion from the Seffle Particles has settled down.

00:17:28.090 --> 00:17:30.450
The remaining enemy ships are taking a pursuit posture.

00:17:31.030 --> 00:17:33.300
They're coming.
Release the heat-sensitive mines.

00:17:33.300 --> 00:17:35.110
Three shots per three minutes.

00:17:35.110 --> 00:17:37.160
We'll keep them at
bay, step by step.

00:17:40.590 --> 00:17:41.690
We've entered the Corridor.

00:17:41.690 --> 00:17:44.010
Enemy ships contacting
the first wave of mines !

00:17:47.110 --> 00:17:48.760
An enemy ship has been destroyed !

00:17:48.760 --> 00:17:50.250
Will that slow them down a bit ?

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:52.350
Other enemy ships are still pursuing.

00:17:53.600 --> 00:17:55.700
There's signs of a ship
in front of us, also.

00:17:56.250 --> 00:17:57.650
There're more enemy ships ?

00:18:00.340 --> 00:18:01.320
It's a friendly ship.

00:18:01.320 --> 00:18:02.710
It's our supply ship !

00:18:04.850 --> 00:18:06.460
Is it just the one supply ship ?

00:18:06.460 --> 00:18:07.620
Are there any escorts ?

00:18:07.620 --> 00:18:08.650
No signs of any.

00:18:10.350 --> 00:18:14.110
It must be the resupply that the Imperial Military Liaison Officer at Phezzan arranged.

00:18:14.110 --> 00:18:18.750
Don't those Fortress idiots have enough
brains to send escorts with a supply ship ?

00:18:19.600 --> 00:18:21.980
The supply ship is starting to retreat !

00:18:21.980 --> 00:18:23.310
What ?

00:18:23.310 --> 00:18:24.810
Are they abandoning us ?

00:18:26.050 --> 00:18:27.620
There's a message
from the supply ship.

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:31.240
It says they'll release the supplies and tells us to catch them.

00:18:31.240 --> 00:18:32.650
That's impossible.

00:18:32.650 --> 00:18:33.980
No, wait.

00:18:35.660 --> 00:18:37.600
With a time series, show me this ship's expected route...

00:18:37.600 --> 00:18:43.080
...as well as the inertial orbit of the supplies released using the present speed of the supply ship.

00:18:52.650 --> 00:18:53.510
I see.

00:18:54.070 --> 00:18:55.090
Captain.

00:18:55.520 --> 00:19:00.010
This way, we can receive the supplies without slowing down our ship in inertial flight.

00:19:00.010 --> 00:19:03.250
Moreover, the slower supply ship can start retreating before us...

00:19:03.250 --> 00:19:05.720
...so it won't slow us 
down after replenishment.

00:19:07.750 --> 00:19:10.020
How unexpected.
This is for the best.

00:19:12.720 --> 00:19:16.660
We'll release all our remaining mines and buy ourselves time to take on supplies.

00:19:16.660 --> 00:19:18.800
All crew members, 
prepare to take on supplies.

00:19:19.550 --> 00:19:22.000
But how exactly
do we retrieve them ?

00:19:23.250 --> 00:19:24.000
By hand.

00:19:29.420 --> 00:19:30.350
He's good.

00:19:31.700 --> 00:19:36.000
I see, so the captain of that supply ship is Lt. Commander Eisenach.

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:37.460
Do you know him ?

00:19:37.460 --> 00:19:39.800
I've never spoken to him.

00:19:39.800 --> 00:19:43.500
But of course, not many 
people have heard his voice.

00:19:43.500 --> 00:19:45.500
He's an extremely reticent man -

00:19:45.500 --> 00:19:48.800
...so much so that he's been tagged with the moniker, "Silent Captain."

00:19:50.230 --> 00:19:51.520
Sounds like an interesting person.

00:20:00.550 --> 00:20:01.830
Alright, let's catch them !

00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:08.660
I've got it !

00:20:09.570 --> 00:20:12.650
Outboard workers, watch out.
Our course will shift.

00:20:16.970 --> 00:20:20.450
The course shifting ratio is 7%.
It's within permissible range.

00:20:20.450 --> 00:20:23.970
No injury to the outboard workers.
They're taking on the supplies steadily.

00:20:24.450 --> 00:20:25.090
Good.

00:20:25.090 --> 00:20:26.970
Hurry up and bring in the supplies.

00:20:26.970 --> 00:20:28.310
Especially the fuel.

00:20:41.900 --> 00:20:43.260
The enemy is being slowed.

00:20:43.680 --> 00:20:44.840
This is a good opportunity.

00:20:44.840 --> 00:20:46.780
Engine, restart !

00:20:46.780 --> 00:20:50.320
The replenishment percentage of energy is still less than 5%, but...

00:20:50.320 --> 00:20:52.600
We can continue to
replenish on the run.

00:20:52.600 --> 00:20:53.700
That's risky !

00:20:53.700 --> 00:20:55.920
There's the possibility that the reactor might melt down...

00:20:55.920 --> 00:20:56.960
It doesn't matter.

00:20:56.960 --> 00:20:59.530
If we break away now,
the enemy will give up.

00:21:02.150 --> 00:21:04.200
As Reinhard asserted...

00:21:04.200 --> 00:21:07.960
...the Alliance force avoided going too deep and gave up on further pursuit.

00:21:09.540 --> 00:21:11.250
Upon returning to Iserlohn Fortress...

00:21:11.250 --> 00:21:14.180
...Reinhard immediately reported to the man who had assigned him to this mission...

00:21:14.180 --> 00:21:16.900
...Rear Admiral Arbentraut.

00:21:17.450 --> 00:21:18.900
You've done a remarkable job.

00:21:18.900 --> 00:21:22.300
But I'm sorry to hear about
Lt. Commander Bendling.

00:21:22.830 --> 00:21:24.970
I have something that the
Lt. Commander left in my custody.

00:21:25.620 --> 00:21:26.720
Huh ?

00:21:26.720 --> 00:21:29.600
The true objective of
this present mission.

00:21:37.650 --> 00:21:38.520
Lord Reinhard.

00:21:39.100 --> 00:21:41.600
The issue has been resolved, Kircheis.

00:21:41.600 --> 00:21:43.050
We'll both get promotions.

00:21:43.590 --> 00:21:45.300
You'll be a Captain next.

00:21:45.300 --> 00:21:48.100
Congratulations on your promotion.

00:21:48.100 --> 00:21:51.650
But I was told to wait
until my 17th birthday.

00:21:51.650 --> 00:21:54.560
Our achievements on this
mission won't be made public.

00:21:54.560 --> 00:21:57.110
They probably need an
excuse for promoting me.

00:21:57.110 --> 00:22:02.520
Besides, we'll have to return to Odin and wait until our next mission is determined.

00:22:03.570 --> 00:22:04.650
By the way...

00:22:04.650 --> 00:22:08.250
...I found out a little about the Imperial Military Liaison Officer at Phezzan who supported us.

00:22:08.250 --> 00:22:09.550
Oh ?

00:22:09.550 --> 00:22:12.700
LTJG Neithart Muller, age 22.

00:22:12.700 --> 00:22:14.550
That's unusually young.

00:22:16.480 --> 00:22:21.340
Kircheis, there are still many 
talents hidden out there.

00:22:22.110 --> 00:22:23.310
Yes.

00:22:23.310 --> 00:22:27.400
Eventually, I'd like to have those talents under my leadership.

00:22:27.400 --> 00:22:30.940
Was it youthfulness that made him
make such a grandiose statement ?

00:22:30.940 --> 00:22:33.800
No, upon the birth of 
a 17 year old Captain...

00:22:33.800 --> 00:22:38.600
...such a statement had the potential to become more than just a dream.

00:22:38.600 --> 00:22:45.150
But they were the only
people who believed in that.

00:22:46.780 --> 00:22:50.250
In January of Imperial Year 484...

00:22:50.250 --> 00:22:54.770
...this voyage of the cruiser, 
Hershrichlenchen, was not recorded.

00:22:54.770 --> 00:22:58.000
And the first use of directional Seffle Particles in battle...

00:22:58.000 --> 00:23:02.900
...was recorded as the
Battle of Amlitzer, three years later.

